// DragRank curated queen dataset.
//
// Hand-curated, not scraped from a live API — placements/seasons sourced
// from Wikipedia, images and wikiUrl verified via the RuPaul's Drag Race
// Fandom wiki's public MediaWiki API (batched lookup with redirect
// following). Images are 640px-wide thumbnails — bumped up
// from an original 184-300px pass once the rating card started
// displaying photos full-bleed at up to 56dvh tall on a retina phone,
// where the small thumbnails looked visibly soft. A handful of newer/
// niche queens have no Fandom page yet — for those, image is null (UI
// falls back to a generated avatar) and wikiUrl points at a Fandom
// search instead of a dead link.
//
// iconicScore has a floor by placement (winner >= 6, runner-up >= 5) so
// franchise winners outside the US aren't buried in the rating queue just
// because they were scored conservatively relative to US mainline queens.
//
// tags vocabulary (2-3 per queen, used by the recommendation engine —
// not shown in the UI): Comedy, HighFashion, Camp, Alternative, Pageant,
// LipsyncAssassin, GirlGroup, Horror, Sweetheart, Villain, Dance, Design,
// BigPersonality, Underdog

